      "sourceTextSha256": "57e9352bb443691d6a8d73e5a1b83f74aa1128f7c9e10207ee77d8f22c339ec4",
      "text": "Duration: 9–10 Hours • Pick Up: 9:00–9:30 am • Language: English and Spanish. Discover Mitla’s intricate stone mosaics, visit a family weaving workshop in Teotitlán del Valle to learn about natural dyes and backstrap weaving, continue to Hierve el Agua to admire mineral formations and panoramic pools, and finish with a mezcal distillery visit including a field-to-glass tasting experience. Included: Shared transportation, certified bilingual guide, entry to archaeological sites and Hierve el Agua, mezcal tasting, overnight in Oaxaca. Not included: Meals, tips, personal expenses.",
